# THETA AI TRADER Development Workflow

## Development Principles

- Every feature must be production-ready.
- Avoid prototype code in production modules.
- Prefer complete implementations over partial scaffolding.
- Keep changes small, focused, and testable.

## Git Workflow

- Make atomic commits with meaningful commit messages.
- Do not commit secrets or `.env` files.
- Keep the main branch stable.

## Testing

- Every production module should have corresponding unit tests.
- Test edge cases and failure scenarios.
- Prefer deterministic tests.

## Documentation

- Public classes and functions require docstrings.
- Update CHANGELOG.md when introducing meaningful features.
- Keep architecture documents in sync with implementation.

## Code Review

Before considering a module complete, verify:
- Correctness
- Readability
- Maintainability
- Performance where appropriate
- Test coverage

## Project Goal

Build THETA AI TRADER as a maintainable, scalable, institutional-grade automated trading platform that can evolve over many years.

